## Summary
Create a Flutter service that wraps the Nearby Connections API for advertising, discovery, and message exchange.

## Tasks
- [ ] Create `NearbyConnectionsService` class in lib/services/
- [ ] Implement advertiser mode (tablet advertises availability)
- [ ] Implement discoverer mode (phone discovers tablets)
- [ ] Implement connection lifecycle (request, accept, reject, disconnect)
- [ ] Implement payload sending/receiving for commands
- [ ] Add connection state management (disconnected, connecting, connected)
- [ ] Handle reconnection on connection loss

## API Design
```dart
class NearbyConnectionsService {
  // Discovery
  Future<void> startAdvertising(String serviceId);
  Future<void> startDiscovery(String serviceId);
  Future<void> stopAdvertising();
  Future<void> stopDiscovery();

  // Connection
  Future<void> requestConnection(String endpointId);
  Future<void> acceptConnection(String endpointId);
  Future<void> rejectConnection(String endpointId);
  Future<void> disconnect(String endpointId);

  // Messaging
  Future<void> sendCommand(String endpointId, RemoteCommand cmd);
  Stream<RemoteCommand> get incomingCommands;

  // State
  Stream<ConnectionState> get connectionState;
  Stream<List<DiscoveredEndpoint>> get discoveredEndpoints;
}
```

## Acceptance Criteria
- Two devices can discover each other
- Devices can establish a connection
- Messages can be sent and received bidirectionally
- Connection state is properly tracked and exposed
